  XML Digital Signer ->
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  In SAP Cloud Integration (CPI), the XML Digital Signer is a step in an iFlow that uses XML
  Signature standard to digitally sign and validate XML messages. This ensures the authenticity
  of the message by guaranteeing the sender's identity and preventing alterations after signing.
  The digital signature is stored as an XML element within the message itself.

  The XML Signature Verifier validates the XML signature contained in the incoming message body and
  returns the content which was signed in the outgoing message body.

